# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored). Placeholders only — NEVER put a real secret here.
# Consumed by apps/web at build time (public, client-exposed values).

PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:4321

# Optional: Cloudflare Web Analytics token (public, not a secret). A production build
# emits the beacon only when this is set; dev builds never do.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# Edge build identifiers (apps/edge). `cf` reads a `.env` file for its own flags
# but does NOT expose those values to `cloudflare.config.ts`, so export them into
# the shell that runs `cf build` / `cf deploy`:
#
#   export CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=<account-id>
#   export SITE_DOMAIN=<domain>
#
# In production both come from the `production-edge` environment's variables, and
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL above must be https:// plus SITE_DOMAIN.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN is a secret: it belongs in the environment secret store only.
